John H. wrote:
> I agree, however, that the various DSMs need more compelling reasons to
> use them.  I also think that DSM is generally overpowered.  I think
> having any equipment object that is obviously a best-of-type passes up
> an opportunity to add strategic depth to the game.

But there isn't a clear best of type, people argue about SDSM vs GDSM
all the time.  There's no reason that everything in a type should be
equally useful; why is it such a bad thing that, say, red DSM isn't
that useful to a character with FR but it's okay that ring mail is
equally useless?

It would be kind of cool to have shimmering DSM, or the proposed gold
DSM, or other useful types.  But there's nothing wrong with some kinds
being clearly inferior, IMO.  Certainly eliminating intrinsic
resistances kind of goes against the entire nethack strategy of
accumulating all possible anti-instadeaths as quickly as possibly, and
it's especially punitive with PR where at relatively low levels orcs
with poison arrows can instadeath at range without regard to Elbereth
or other tactical options that you normally have for avoiding
instadeath.



